    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted"><strong>Touch Grass Simulator</strong> &middot; published by Maffin<br />Effective date: 6 June 2026</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information the mobile game <strong>Touch Grass Simulator</strong> (the &ldquo;Game&rdquo;) collects, how it is used, and the choices you have. By installing or playing the Game, you agree to this policy.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>The Game does <strong>not</strong> require you to create an account or provide your name, email, or other directly identifying details. We and our service providers may collect the following automatically:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Device &amp; technical data:</strong> device model, operating-system version, language, and a mobile <strong>advertising identifier</strong> (e.g. Google Advertising ID).</li>
        <li><strong>Network data:</strong> IP address and an approximate (city/country-level) location derived from it.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage &amp; diagnostics:</strong> in-game events, performance data, and crash reports.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchase data:</strong> records of in-app purchases. Payments are processed by Google Play; we do <strong>not</strong> receive your full payment-card details.</li>
        <li><strong>Saved game progress:</strong> stored in the cloud and tied to an anonymous identifier so it can sync across your sessions and devices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To run, save, and improve the Game and your progress.</li>
        <li>To display and measure advertising, including frequency capping and reward delivery.</li>
        <li>To process and validate in-app purchases.</li>
        <li>To analyse performance, fix crashes, and prevent fraud and abuse.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
    <p>The Game shows ads through <strong>Unity LevelPlay</strong> (ironSource) mediation, which may serve ads from third-party networks (for example Google AdMob, Unity Ads, AppLovin, and Meta Audience Network). These partners use the advertising identifier and the data above to deliver personalized or non-personalized ads and to measure their performance.</p>
    <p>You can limit ad tracking at any time by resetting or deleting your advertising ID in <em>Android Settings &rarr; Privacy &rarr; Ads</em>. Players in the EEA, UK, and other applicable regions are shown a consent prompt and can change their choice at any time.</p>

    <h2>4. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Unity Technologies (Unity Gaming Services, LevelPlay, Analytics) &mdash; <a href="https://unity.com/legal/privacy-policy">unity.com/legal/privacy-policy</a></li>
        <li>ironSource / Unity LevelPlay &mdash; <a href="https://www.is.com/privacy-policy/">is.com/privacy-policy</a></li>
        <li>Google (Play services, AdMob, Play Billing) &mdash; <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a></li>
        <li>AppLovin &mdash; <a href="https://www.applovin.com/privacy/">applovin.com/privacy</a></li>
        <li>Meta Audience Network &mdash; <a href="https://www.facebook.com/about/privacy">facebook.com/about/privacy</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We share the data above only with the service providers listed here so they can perform their functions (serving ads, saving progress, processing purchases), and where required by law.</p>

    <h2>6. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
    <p>We keep data only as long as needed for the purposes above. You can clear your local data by uninstalling the Game or resetting progress in its settings. To request deletion of cloud-saved data tied to your identifier, contact us at the address below.</p>

    <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>The Game is not directed to children under 13 (or under 16 in the EEA), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

    <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict processing of your personal data, to object to processing, to data portability, and (for California residents) to opt out of the &ldquo;sale&rdquo; or &ldquo;sharing&rdquo; of personal information. To exercise these rights, contact us below.</p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>Data is transmitted over encrypted (HTTPS) connections and our providers apply industry-standard safeguards. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, however, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>10. International Transfers</h2>
    <p>Your information may be processed on servers outside your country. Where required, our providers use appropriate safeguards for such transfers.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by updating the &ldquo;Effective date&rdquo; above.</p>

    <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
        Questions or requests regarding this policy or your data:<br />
        <strong>Maffin</strong><br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:support@yourdomain.com">support@yourdomain.com</a>
    </p>
</body>
